Oh, you want to know what they are?

























Well AFAIK, this list isn't exhaustive, but it's a start:

You mentioned prayer and normal level gain.

Quaffing non-cursed potions of healing can increase maximum hit points. 
Blessed is better, and the better the potion the better. You generally need 
to be at or near full hit points. AFAIK, diluted potions are as good as 
undiluted. This is my preferred method of hit point increase - using 
alchemy means I can get several hundred hit points relatively simply before 
entering Gehennom.

Nurses will heal damage and can increase hit points if they hit you when 
you are unarmed and unarmoured (take off all your armour and unwield your 
weapon). This can be dangerous, particularly if you forget to put vital 
items of clothing back on afterwards. I avoid this method.

Things that grant instant level increases (!oGL, foocubi, wraith corpses) 
will increase hit points (and mana IIRC) if you use them when you are 
already level 30. As I generally avoid being as high as level 30, I avoid 
this method too.


